A||||1||ThatRickGuy||Ocealet & cat eliminator review||||1||
Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||06-08-2001||09:16 AM||||Hey everyone, I finally got the new exhaust on last night, just thought I'd post my findings.<P>New sound: louder, not as deep as I would have liked, but still nice. Not too bad from inside the cabin, but with the windows down, you probrably wont be able to hear your sterio at WOT acceleration.<P>Install: Not too bad, one this though, the cat eliminator pipe from the fiero store needs a little work, the yoak where it mates up w/ the y-pipe was the problem. the holes for the bolts are just large enough for the bolts to slide threw, unfortunatly the were not perfectly aligned, so when I tried to bolt up the exhaust there was an 1/8 in. gap. I took about 20 minutes w/ a round file and opened them up, about 1/8-1/4 in towards the pipe and away. I still have a little leak, I can barily feel with my hand, another 10 minutes with the file would have fixed it though. So, if you use this pipe, do your self a favor and file out the openings first.<P>Performance: Seems like mid/high RPM range power has been significatly improved over the mostlikely original stock exhaust. I don't have a G-tec and I'm not going to splurg on a dyno so I can't give you any numbers, but between the ported manifolds and the new exhaust, it's definately got better throtle responce and mid/high RPM range power.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dave Gunsul||06-08-2001||11:32 AM||||I've got the same set-up on my GT but I made the cat replacement pipe myself.<BR>Topend is improved but I thought it was very deep sounding and not quite loud enough.<BR>Friends say it really sounds good and they can hear me coming so maybe it's just me but<BR>I really can't hear it when idleing next to other cars. Sounds good taking off though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>My new engine has headers so maybe that will make it loud enough for me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
